---
import Layout from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy: High Signal Podcasts"
  description="Privacy notes and data boundaries for the public High Signal Podcasts evidence index."
  breadcrumb={[{ name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy' }]}
>
  <section class="info-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notes</p>
    <h1>The public index does not need a reader account.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Browsing, searching, and using the public read-only API currently require no signup. The
      product does not ask readers to create a profile or submit private podcast material.
    </p>
    <div class="info-grid">
      <article><p class="folio">Corpus / 01</p><h2>Public-source records.</h2><p>Published claims come from public podcast sources and retain attribution and source links so readers can inspect the record.</p></article>
      <article><p class="folio">Access / 02</p><h2>No public write path.</h2><p>The public API is read-only. Administrative ingestion and review routes are protected and are not reader-facing product surfaces.</p></article>
      <article><p class="folio">Site analytics / 03</p><h2>Pseudonymous usage events.</h2><p>App Health receives page visits and named actions such as searching the archive or opening an evidence receipt. These named events include no search text, form contents, or personal profile data.</p></article>
      <article><p class="folio">Shared surfaces / 04</p><h2>Fleet navigation and Ask AI.</h2><p>The footer loads shared SaaS Maker navigation, Ask AI, and a newsletter form. The newsletter is optional and asks for consent before submission; its privacy details are linked in the form.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="info-note">For a correction or privacy question about an indexed record, use the project’s public GitHub issue tracker.</p>
    <div class="info-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/Significant-Hobbies/on-record/issues">Raise a question ↗</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/sources">Inspect the source index</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
